in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes 3 attempts in total, waiting 0.5s after the first failure and 1s after the second. If the third attempt also gets a 503, the original `HTTPError` is raised as before.\n\n- **Only 503 is retried.** Other HTTP errors and network errors are raised straight away, unchanged.\n- **New constructor option:** `sleep` (defaults to `time.sleep`), so tests can skip the real waits. The attempt count and backoff are class constants, `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3` and `BACKOFF_BASE = 0.5`.\n\nI tested it against a throwaway local HTTP server; the repo has no test suite and I didn't add one. All four cases behaved as intended:\n\n| Server responses | Requests | Waits | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | 3 | 0.5s, 1.0s | Data returned |\n| 503, 503, 503 | 3 | 0.5s, 1.0s | `HTTPError 503` |\n| 500 | 1 | none | `HTTPError 500` |\n| 200 | 1 | none | Data returned |", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 34694, "requests_cache_write": 143594, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7585968, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1682, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial12", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 83, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:48:54.839008+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 19.519, "t_checker_s": 5.435, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1694, "tokens_cache_read": 34694, "tokens_cache_write": 143594